d","passed":true,"violation_count":0,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905794719","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905794719","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2026-04-20","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-960968-i20260416","date":"2026-04-16","inspection_type":"Investigation of a report","result":"Deficiencies cited","passed":false,"violation_count":8,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905921596","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905921596","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2026-04-16","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[{"id":"tx-hhsc-960968-i20260416-v1","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-305-a-1","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-960968-i20260416","date":"2026-04-16","original_code":"746.305(a)(1)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2026-06-01","finding":"Report Unsafe Facility Occurrence: The operation failed to notify licensing of significant water damage and visible mold growth throughout the facility that created an unsafe and unsanitary environment.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026570178","violation_type_title":"Report Unsafe Facility Occurrence (26 TAC §746.305(a)(1))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-960968-i20260416-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1003-1","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-960968-i20260416","date":"2026-04-16","original_code":"746.1003(1)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2026-06-01","finding":"Director Responsibilities - Operate in Compliance: The director failed ensure timely repairs were made, which led to the development of mold within the operation.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026570180","violation_type_title":"Director Responsibilities - Operate in Compliance (26 TAC §746.1003(1))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-960968-i20260416-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3301-b","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-960968-i20260416","date":"2026-04-16","original_code":"746.3301(b)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2026-06-01","finding":"Nutrition and Food Service - Follow Meal Patterns: Based on evidence gathered throughout the investigation, it was determined that the operation did not follow the meal patterns established by the U.S. Department of Agriculture Child and Adult Care Food Program.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026570182","violation_type_title":"Nutrition and Food Service - Follow Meal Patterns (26 TAC §746.3301(b))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-960968-i20260416-v4","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1201-1","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-960968-i20260416","date":"2026-04-16","original_code":"746.1201(1)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2026-06-01","finding":"Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Demonstrate Competency, Good Judgment, Self-control: The operation failed to show good judgment and competency when continuing to provide care in an unsafe and unsanitary environment.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026570176","violation_type_title":"Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Demonstrate Competency, Good Judgment, Self-control (26 TAC §746.1201(1))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-960968-i20260416-v5","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3407-9","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-960968-i20260416","date":"2026-04-16","original_code":"746.3407(9)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2026-06-01","finding":"Floors, ceilings and Walls in Good Repair and Clean: Extensive mold and water damage was observed in four classrooms within the operation. Carpets were observed saturated with water, and visible mold growth (green, blue, and black in color) was present along the walls. The classroom doorways were covered with black plastic that had been stapled in place, restricting access to see those areas. Ceiling tiles had fallen from the roof and remained on the floor without being cleaned up. Additionally, large trash cans and plastic wading pools were placed underneath open ceiling in some of the classrooms with standing water inside. These conditions reflect a significantly unsafe and unsanitary environment.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026570181","violation_type_title":"Floors, ceilings and Walls in Good Repair and Clean (26 TAC §746.3407(9))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-960968-i20260416-v6","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-4751-b","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-960968-i20260416","date":"2026-04-16","original_code":"746.4751(b)","severity":"medium","severity_label":"Medium risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2026-06-01","finding":"Maintenance Procedures for Active Play - Monthly Maintenance Checklist: Based on evidence gathered throughout the investigation, it was determined that the operation failed to remove glass from the playground after a vehicle was crashed into the area.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026570179","violation_type_title":"Maintenance Procedures for Active Play - Monthly Maintenance Checklist (26 TAC §746.4751(b))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-960968-i20260416-v7","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-201-9","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-960968-i20260416","date":"2026-04-16","original_code":"746.201(9)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2026-06-01","finding":"Complying with Laws and Rules: The permit holder failed to ensure building maintenance and repairs were made in a timely manner, which resulted in significant water damage and the development of mold throughout the facility.     The permit holder also failed to ensure child care regulation was notified of the unsafe and unsanitary environment of the facility.     Additionally, the permit holder allowed children to continue receiving care in the operation despite the building being in these unsafe and unsanitary conditions.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026570177","violation_type_title":"Complying with Laws and Rules (26 TAC §746.201(9))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-960968-i20260416-v8","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3301-g","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-960968-i20260416","date":"2026-04-16","original_code":"746.3301(g)","severity":"medium","severity_label":"Medium risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2026-06-01","finding":"Nutrition and Food Service - No Beverages with Added Sugar, unless allowed by CACFP: Based on evidence gathered throughout the investigation, it has been determined that the operation severed the children in care sugary beverages for several days.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026570175","violation_type_title":"Nutrition and Food Service - No Beverages with Added Sugar, unless allowed by CACFP (26 TAC §746.3301(g))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"}]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-960968-i20251112","date":"2025-11-12","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"No deficiencies cited","passed":true,"violation_count":0,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905794718","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905794718","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2025-11-12","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-960968-i20251028","date":"2025-10-28","inspection_type":"Invest